1
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,800
"Blue Lips"

2
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:13,800
(Episode 15)

3
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:15,960
Shixian,

4
00:01:17,059 --> 00:01:18,539
you need to keep studying.

5
00:01:19,539 --> 00:01:20,639
Next semester,

6
00:01:21,199 --> 00:01:22,800
you'll go back and make up your classes.

7
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:24,980
Got it?

8
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:26,880
Okay.

9
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:27,960
Sis,

10
00:01:28,639 --> 00:01:30,159
I'll study hard.

11
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:32,480
And Shixian,

12
00:01:34,699 --> 00:01:37,380
I've never seen the
ocean in my entire life.

13
00:01:38,579 --> 00:01:40,460
Go see it for me.

14
00:01:42,199 --> 00:01:44,579
Scatter my ashes in the sea.

15
00:01:46,539 --> 00:01:48,960
Let me follow the rivers and oceans

16
00:01:49,739 --> 00:01:51,440
to see this world.

17
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:54,460
Sis,

18
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,539
you'll promise me, right?

19
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,400
Okay.

20
00:02:01,139 --> 00:02:02,139
I promise you.

21
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:04,699
I'll take you to see the ocean.

22
00:02:11,539 --> 00:02:12,539
Shixian,

23
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:14,860
look.

24
00:02:16,599 --> 00:02:18,940
The sunset is so beautiful today.

25
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:23,719
Tomorrow will definitely
be a beautiful, sunny day.

26
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:32,860
A day in heaven

27
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:34,719
is ten years on earth.

28
00:02:38,179 --> 00:02:39,599
Take your time joining me.

29
00:02:41,059 --> 00:02:42,639
Live a good life.

30
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,239
If you come too early,

31
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:47,659
I'm going to punish you.

32
00:02:48,599 --> 00:02:49,599
Got it?

33
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,039
I got it, Sis.

34
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:03,280
Shixian,

35
00:03:05,659 --> 00:03:07,400
I'm a little tired.

36
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:10,460
I want to sleep.

37
00:03:15,679 --> 00:03:16,719
Shixian,

38
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:20,460
stay safe and healthy.

39
00:03:21,739 --> 00:03:23,260
Live a long, long life.

40
00:03:27,199 --> 00:03:28,199
Sis,

41
00:03:30,539 --> 00:03:32,400
let me sing you a song.

42
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:33,760
Just treat it

43
00:03:35,699 --> 00:03:37,480
as a lullaby to put you to sleep.

44
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:38,760
Okay?

45
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,400
Okay.

46
00:03:41,519 --> 00:03:44,559
It's been so long since I heard you sing.

47
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:58,420
The late-night platform is so quiet.

48
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:01,340
Only the wind is listening.

49
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:05,440
You're carrying an old suitcase,

50
00:04:06,199 --> 00:04:08,800
saying you're going on a trip.

51
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:11,019
Go on.

52
00:04:11,739 --> 00:04:12,880
Go on.

53
00:04:13,519 --> 00:04:16,679
The distant lights are still shining.

54
00:04:17,579 --> 00:04:20,960
Go on, go on.

55
00:05:14,619 --> 00:05:15,619
Hello?

56
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,239
Is this Mr. Teng?

57
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:19,280
This is Qi Yu from Bojin Law Firm.

58
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:22,860
Do you remember Gu Duoer's
case from five years ago?

59
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:25,219
We've reopened the investigation.

60
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:26,820
I believe

61
00:05:27,119 --> 00:05:28,239
you might have

62
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:30,280
some clues we need.

63
00:05:31,099 --> 00:05:33,579
Would you be willing to
cooperate with our investigation?

64
00:05:35,679 --> 00:05:36,920
Sis.

65
00:05:47,639 --> 00:05:48,639
Mr. Teng.

66
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:49,880
Mr. Teng.

67
00:08:01,199 --> 00:08:02,199
Sis.

68
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:05,239
Teng Mo said from now on,

69
00:08:07,059 --> 00:08:09,219
you are the cherry blossoms
on the branches in spring.

70
00:08:10,820 --> 00:08:12,699
You are the cool breeze on a summer night.

71
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:16,659
You are the first rain of autumn.

72
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:20,539
The first breath of warm air in winter

73
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:22,380
is also you.

74
00:08:25,199 --> 00:08:27,199
The notes played on the guitar strings

75
00:08:27,859 --> 00:08:29,159
are you singing.

76
00:08:31,239 --> 00:08:32,579
The starry sky

77
00:08:33,239 --> 00:08:34,439
is you watching me.

78
00:08:37,460 --> 00:08:39,140
Even though we can't see each other again,

79
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,819
you'll still be by my side.

80
00:08:43,859 --> 00:08:44,859
Sis,

81
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:46,920
don't worry.

82
00:08:47,939 --> 00:08:49,659
I'll live a good life with Teng Mo.

83
00:08:50,619 --> 00:08:52,119
I'll live for you too,

84
00:08:53,979 --> 00:08:55,159
and live well.

85
00:09:01,279 --> 00:09:02,420
What do you want for dinner?

86
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
I'll make it for you.

87
00:09:09,119 --> 00:09:10,439
I don't have much of an appetite.

88
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:15,760
Get some good rest for the next few days.

89
00:09:16,659 --> 00:09:18,079
Leave the rest to me.

90
00:09:19,819 --> 00:09:21,219
I was going to wait until
your sister got better.

91
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:22,220
Okay.

92
00:09:35,119 --> 00:09:36,119
Alright then.

93
00:10:00,899 --> 00:10:02,036
This is the application for readmission.

94
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:02,600
Fill it out.

95
00:10:03,079 --> 00:10:04,999
There are also the
suspension records and forms.

96
00:10:05,260 --> 00:10:06,820
We'll mail them to the school tomorrow.

97
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,938
Your hair.

98
00:10:11,939 --> 00:10:14,259
It's probably not appropriate
to have it blue for college.

99
00:10:15,380 --> 00:10:16,900
I'll take you to dye it back tomorrow.

100
00:10:17,039 --> 00:10:19,239
And then we'll get you a
more handsome haircut.

101
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:22,020
Okay.

102
00:10:22,399 --> 00:10:23,399
By the way, Shixian,

103
00:10:24,039 --> 00:10:25,799
I have something I
want to discuss with you.

104
00:10:27,079 --> 00:10:28,079
Go ahead.

105
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:30,579
I want to open another shop.

106
00:10:31,239 --> 00:10:33,520
There's a perfect storefront
on the pedestrian street.

107
00:10:33,659 --> 00:10:34,659
I want to take it over

108
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,000
and turn it into a coffee shop.

109
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:47,899
The money you gave me before,

110
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:49,300
I've saved it all.

111
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:51,600
There's still some left

112
00:10:52,119 --> 00:10:54,100
after deducting my
sister's medical expenses.

113
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:55,880
I've transferred it all in.

114
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:57,880
You keep it.

115
00:10:58,020 --> 00:11:00,000
You'll need it for college
and making friends.

116
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:02,340
You take it.

117
00:11:04,659 --> 00:11:05,520
Originally, this money

118
00:11:05,521 --> 00:11:07,300
was for my sister's surgery.

119
00:11:08,079 --> 00:11:09,399
Now it's not needed.

120
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:14,825
Just consider it as
my sister investing in your coffee shop.

121
00:11:15,579 --> 00:11:16,579
I believe

122
00:11:17,399 --> 00:11:18,779
she would definitely agree.

123
00:11:23,539 --> 00:11:26,039
She always wanted to have her own business.

124
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,039
Just think of it

125
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:30,939
as you fulfilling her wish for her.

126
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:34,760
Then tell me,

127
00:11:35,439 --> 00:11:37,560
what should we name our coffee shop?

128
00:11:39,479 --> 00:11:40,479
Anything is fine.

129
00:11:41,020 --> 00:11:42,020
What do you think?

130
00:11:43,399 --> 00:11:44,399
Then let's call it.

131
00:11:44,619 --> 00:11:45,720
Blue Lips.

132
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:51,539
Blue Lips.

133
00:11:53,899 --> 00:11:54,899
That's pretty good.

134
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:57,260
In the future,

135
00:11:57,479 --> 00:11:58,640
our coffee shop

136
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:00,460
will be decorated very cozily.

137
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:03,319
We'll fill it with all kinds of plants.

138
00:12:03,439 --> 00:12:05,100
And we'll play the songs you like.

139
00:12:07,739 --> 00:12:09,779
What about your old place?

140
00:12:10,199 --> 00:12:11,199
I gave it up.

141
00:12:14,739 --> 00:12:16,239
I actually really liked it there.

142
00:12:17,020 --> 00:12:18,039
Then I won't give it up.

143
00:12:23,220 --> 00:12:24,220
Shixian,

144
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,359
I have two more things to tell you.

145
00:12:31,779 --> 00:12:33,500
I want to introduce you to my parents.

146
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:37,760
Your parents?

147
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:46,140
Will they

148
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:48,220
be able to accept me?

149
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,079
My parents are a bit traditional,

150
00:13:00,039 --> 00:13:01,039
but they

151
00:13:01,199 --> 00:13:02,699
are both kind-hearted people.

152
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:03,920
Besides,

153
00:13:04,140 --> 00:13:05,140
you're so great,

154
00:13:05,399 --> 00:13:06,399
who wouldn't like you?

155
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:08,800
What if they find out

156
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,560
where we met?

157
00:13:12,539 --> 00:13:14,819
We don't need to share every little detail.

158
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:16,560
Silly.

159
00:13:19,439 --> 00:13:20,039
Alright.

160
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:21,420
Come here.

161
00:13:23,579 --> 00:13:24,000
This one.

162
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:25,920
Let's start from here.

163
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:35,840
What are you doing?

164
00:13:36,039 --> 00:13:37,039
Are we moving?

165
00:13:37,979 --> 00:13:39,159
I'm picking out clothes.

166
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:41,300
Which one do you think I should wear?

167
00:13:41,812 --> 00:13:42,812
Is it hot in Fengzhou?

168
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:44,738
Should I wear a shirt,

169
00:13:44,739 --> 00:13:45,760
or a sweater?

170
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,460
Is a leather jacket a bit

171
00:13:48,739 --> 00:13:49,739
too aggressive?

172
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:51,899
Just get a couple of shirts.

173
00:13:51,979 --> 00:13:53,499
They won't know the difference anyway.

174
00:13:55,079 --> 00:13:55,460
No way.

175
00:13:55,659 --> 00:13:57,279
A black shirt definitely won't work.

176
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:58,860
It has to be a white shirt, right?

177
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:02,300
Taking this meet-the-parents
thing pretty seriously, huh?

178
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:03,800
Of course.

179
00:14:03,979 --> 00:14:05,260
I have to leave them with a

180
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:06,859
good first impression.

181
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:10,100
You might not even like
them when you get there.

182
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:11,260
Impossible.

183
00:14:11,619 --> 00:14:12,619
Definitely not.

184
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:13,920
Why?

185
00:14:14,819 --> 00:14:15,819
Because

186
00:14:17,359 --> 00:14:18,818
they are your parents, after all.

187
00:14:18,819 --> 00:14:20,399
How could I not like them?

188
00:14:22,340 --> 00:14:23,340
Shixian,

189
00:14:23,859 --> 00:14:25,659
everyone has a lot of flaws.

190
00:14:26,199 --> 00:14:28,039
I have many flaws my parents don't like,

191
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:30,100
and it's the same for me with them.

192
00:14:31,279 --> 00:14:33,000
But because we're family,

193
00:14:33,159 --> 00:14:34,399
none of that matters.

194
00:14:34,619 --> 00:14:36,199
Just be your true self.

195
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,000
I'm just afraid

196
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:42,380
what if they don't approve?

197
00:14:43,300 --> 00:14:44,980
If they don't approve, they don't approve.

198
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:46,816
It's not like they're
the ones living with you.

199
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:47,840
Besides,

200
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:49,659
we'll have tried our best.

201
00:14:49,779 --> 00:14:51,316
As long as we have a
clear conscience, it's fine.

202
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:53,380
You might even change
your mind when you get there.

203
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,600
Don't talk nonsense.

204
00:14:57,199 --> 00:14:58,199
I think

205
00:14:58,300 --> 00:14:59,420
these two look pretty good.

206
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:02,340
This one goes perfectly
with the denim jacket.

207
00:15:02,899 --> 00:15:04,979
Middle-aged and older
women will absolutely love it.

208
00:15:05,439 --> 00:15:06,439
This is the one.

209
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:07,960
Are you sure?

210
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:09,180
Let's just go with this.

211
00:15:09,359 --> 00:15:10,359
Let's go. Time to eat.

212
00:15:26,159 --> 00:15:27,159
Is my hair messy?

213
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:30,800
You look super handsome.

214
00:15:32,619 --> 00:15:33,619
Let's go.

215
00:15:41,979 --> 00:15:42,979
Dad.

216
00:15:43,079 --> 00:15:44,079
Mom.

217
00:15:44,939 --> 00:15:45,939
Hello, Uncle.

218
00:15:47,359 --> 00:15:47,979
You're back.

219
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:49,340
Hello, Auntie.

220
00:15:49,439 --> 00:15:51,079
These are local specialties from Jinyang.

221
00:15:51,359 --> 00:15:52,839
I brought these specifically for you.

222
00:15:52,979 --> 00:15:53,659
Some nutritional supplements.
Thank you so much.

223
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:55,399
Come, have a seat.

224
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:56,760
Okay.

225
00:15:58,739 --> 00:15:59,659
What would you like to drink?

226
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:00,720
I'll go pour it for you.

227
00:16:01,199 --> 00:16:02,260
Auntie, I'm not thirsty.

228
00:16:03,119 --> 00:16:03,539
Well...

229
00:16:03,699 --> 00:16:05,059
Mo-mo, entertain our guest for a bit.

230
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:06,340
I still have some cooking to do.

231
00:16:06,399 --> 00:16:07,399
Have a seat.

232
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:11,060
Dad.
How about this?

233
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:12,699
You guys chat.

234
00:16:13,039 --> 00:16:14,879
I'll go see what delicious
food Mom is making.

235
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:24,520
Uncle.

236
00:16:24,819 --> 00:16:27,300
I heard you grew all these flowers.

237
00:16:27,460 --> 00:16:28,620
They're absolutely beautiful.

238
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:31,460
Yes, yes, I grew them.

239
00:16:43,479 --> 00:16:43,960
Uncle.

240
00:16:44,119 --> 00:16:45,618
Teng Mo always tells me

241
00:16:45,619 --> 00:16:47,539
that you're amazing
at raising tropical fish.

242
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:51,100
It's not too bad, I guess.

243
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:01,899
Come on.

244
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:03,779
Let me show you my room.

245
00:17:25,439 --> 00:17:26,439
What's wrong?

246
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:29,760
Nothing.

247
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:31,720
If it's nothing, why do
you look so unhappy?

248
00:17:32,619 --> 00:17:33,819
I'm not unhappy.

249
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:36,960
You think I can't tell when you're unhappy?

250
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:42,359
Should I

251
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:43,880
not have come?

252
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:45,640
No way.

253
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:47,576
My parents have been waiting for you.

254
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:47,960
See?

255
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:49,500
You're lying again.

256
00:17:53,779 --> 00:17:54,779
I can tell.

257
00:17:57,800 --> 00:17:58,800
What can you tell?

258
00:18:04,739 --> 00:18:05,739
Forget it.

259
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:07,140
Anyway,

260
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:08,880
this is the only time I'll be here.

261
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:11,060
Come on.

262
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:13,880
Give me a smile.

263
00:18:30,579 --> 00:18:31,800
Come on, dinner's ready!

264
00:18:36,819 --> 00:18:37,819
This is...

265
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:40,539
My mom made this especially for you.

266
00:18:41,380 --> 00:18:42,380
I thought

267
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:44,160
people in Fengzhou didn't eat spicy food.

268
00:18:44,319 --> 00:18:45,319
We don't.

269
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:46,875
She just learned how to make this.

270
00:18:46,899 --> 00:18:48,039
She found a video online.

271
00:18:48,279 --> 00:18:50,199
She even asked me which
chili sauce is the best.

272
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:51,715
Jinyang peppers are hard to stir-fry,

273
00:18:51,739 --> 00:18:53,439
so I bought her some ready-made ones.

274
00:18:57,359 --> 00:18:58,779
Eat up, eat up.

275
00:19:00,020 --> 00:19:01,020
Try this.

276
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,060
Mo-mo

277
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:07,539
told us all about your situation.

278
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:10,540
You and your sister have had it rough.

279
00:19:17,119 --> 00:19:18,119
Ms. Hu,

280
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:20,420
it's rare to see you so emotional.

281
00:19:22,119 --> 00:19:23,179
Don't act like that in front of Shixian.

282
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:24,180
Show some respect.

283
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,000
Anyway,

284
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:29,180
make yourself at home.

285
00:19:29,359 --> 00:19:30,800
Treat this like your own home.

286
00:19:34,539 --> 00:19:35,539
Hurry and try it.

287
00:19:43,539 --> 00:19:44,539
Is it good?

288
00:19:46,039 --> 00:19:47,039
It's delicious.

289
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:50,739
This kid Teng Mo,

290
00:19:50,939 --> 00:19:52,659
sometimes he speaks without thinking.

291
00:19:52,939 --> 00:19:54,299
You can't indulge his bad habits.

292
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:55,300
You hear me?

293
00:19:58,180 --> 00:19:59,180
Mom,

294
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:00,740
don't take this chance to smear me.

295
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:03,460
Your son still has
plenty of good qualities.

296
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:08,300
I think Teng Mo is pretty great.

297
00:20:08,779 --> 00:20:09,520
Usually,

298
00:20:09,739 --> 00:20:10,760
he's very reliable.

299
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,000
And

300
00:20:12,079 --> 00:20:13,319
he's really funny to talk to.

301
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:14,960
He's quite interesting.

302
00:20:19,119 --> 00:20:19,800
Why are you looking at me?
Is he wrong?

303
00:20:24,399 --> 00:20:26,300
Beauty truly is in the eye of the beholder.

304
00:20:28,939 --> 00:20:29,520
Hurry up and eat.

305
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:30,920
Eat up, take big bites.

306
00:20:32,479 --> 00:20:33,479
Here, try this.

307
00:20:34,819 --> 00:20:36,180
Come on, try this duck intestine.

308
00:20:36,319 --> 00:20:37,319
Thank you, Auntie.

309
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:38,960
Eat up.
